<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Save-Path Invariants — IslandAdaptor Outbound

Path K / F-arc: outbound hygiene for sustained live wiki authoring.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/problem>>

!! Problem Space

`IslandAdaptor.saveTiddler` acts as the boundary where TW5 wiki edits cross
into the Automerge store. Without hygiene here, sustained editing produces:

* ''Write amplification'' — every keystroke fires a store write + CRDT patch +
  disk-projector file write. At 5 keystrokes/sec over a 10-minute session:
  3 000 store writes, 3 000 disk writes, all for the same tiddler.
* ''Noisy projection state'' — parse-warning tiddlers, `$:/state/*` fragments,
  and boot-splash signals accumulate in the wiki. Some carry `lar:` URIs and
  could bleed into the store without guards.
* ''Draft routing confusion'' — draft tiddlers from TW5 editing UX
  should reach the per-wiki draft bag, not get silently dropped.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/invariants>>

!! Invariants

!!! SP-1 — Capture Debounce

`saveTiddler` MUST debounce per title. The debounce window: ''400 ms''.

* While the timer runs, subsequent saves for the same title cancel the
  prior timer and restart it with the latest fields.
* The returned promise settles once per debounce window — at flush time, not
  at call time; a superseded save's promise resolves when the next one takes
  its place. Callers MUST tolerate asynchronous settlement.
* `stop()` MUST cancel all pending timers and drop pending writes without
  flushing them.

Rationale: human keystroke rate typically runs 3–8 chars/sec. A 400 ms window
coalesces a full word or short phrase into a single store write. Stays below
perceived lag threshold (< 1 s).

!!! SP-2 — Ephemeral Truncation

The VOLATILE VM PLANE (`lar:///lararium.local.vm/…`, `VOLATILE_VM_PREFIX` in
`packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts`) MUST NOT reach the Automerge store.
`saveTiddler` and `deleteTiddler` refuse it by `isVolatileVmUri`, ahead of the
cascade, so no cascade edit can lift the refusal (`island-adaptor.ts`).

Every OTHER title a wiki write touches reaches `saveTiddler`: the outbound
bridge carries each live `change`, whichever door wrote it, and the cascade's
`[prefix[lar:]]` rule routes a `lar:` title to `current-wiki-bag`. So wiki
scratch that must stay off the store lives under the volatile plane; a scratch
title spelled anywhere else (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/state/…`, a parse-warning title)
persists like any authored tiddler.

Auto-truncate sweep: a separate sweeper (outside this adaptor) MAY scan the
TW5 wiki on a low-frequency timer (≥ 30 s idle) and delete stale
parse-warning tiddlers. The adaptor owns the debounce; sweep lives in a
TW5 startup module.

!!! SP-3 — Draft Routing

Draft tiddlers from TW5 editing UX (a `draft.of` field standing) MUST route to the wiki's per-wiki
draft slot (`wikis/{slug}/draft`, a CRDT layer that follows the operator's fleet)
and MUST NOT be silently dropped. The in-wiki bag-paths cascade carries the rule
(`[is[draft]then{…/current-wiki-draft}]`), read against TW5's `draft.of` FIELD,
never the title; the matching delete routes by the last-known-slot map
(`_slotOf`), since the field has gone by then. No guard in `saveTiddler` withholds a
draft. The cascade names its withholdings (`$:/core`, `$:/library/sjcl.js`) and
ends in a catch-all — a title no rule reaches lands at the write layer and says
so (wiki-layer-ontology#/totality-law). The measured routing table rides
recipe-layer-model#/as-routed.

!!! SP-4 — Ceremony Routing

No persisted field names a bag. Residency rides the ENVELOPE: the store fires
each change with its own bag, the nalu stamps `$origin-bag` on the wiki side for
the projector, and the outbound save strips that stamp before the put. `bag`
stays the author's own field and never routes. A ceremony that targets one
specific bag (MOVE, promotion, `meme put --bag`) carries the bag on the put
OPTION (`store.put(record, origin, { bag })`) — never on the record — and a
bag with no writable layer refuses loud rather than falling through to the
default writable (wiki-layer-ontology#/write-law).

Live TW5 edits route by the cascade: `_destination(title)` names the slot, and the put carries it as the `{ bag }` option.

!!! SP-5 — Single Parser Law

All inbound meme text passes through `splitBodyTiddler()` (ONE parser,
FOUR call sites law). `_writeMeme` upholds this; do not add a second parse
site.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/debounce-design>>

!! Debounce Design

```
saveTiddler(tiddler): Promise<void>
  → guards (echo · the volatile VM plane · the cascade's named withholdings)
  → cancel pending timer for title; resolve the superseded promise
  → store { fields, resolve, reject, origin } in _pending map
  → set new timer(400ms) → _flushPending(title)

_flushPending(title)
  → retrieve + delete from _pending
  → call _writeMeme(title, fields, origin)
  → settle the promise on resolve/reject
```

State held on the adaptor:

| Field | Type | Lifecycle |
|---|---|---|
| `_debounce` | `Map<string, TimerHandle>` | per pending title; cleared on stop() |
| `_pending` | `Map<string, PendingWrite>` | tracks latest fields + callback per title |

`PendingWrite`:
```ts
{ fields: Record<string, string>; resolve: () => void; reject: (err: Error) => void; origin: ChangeOrigin }
```

On `stop()`: iterate `_debounce`, clearTimeout each, clear both maps and the
inbound echo SET, and unsubscribe from the projection bus. No write flushes
after `stop()`.

<<~/ahu>>

